## DEFINITION
PSIPRED is a bioinformatics tool used to predict the secondary structure of proteins from their amino acid sequences.

## PURPOSE
- Predict protein secondary structure.
- Identify structural elements.
- Support protein function analysis.
- Assist in protein structure modeling.

## STRUCTURE PREDICTED
- Alpha helices (α-helices)
- Beta strands (β-sheets)
- Random coils (loops)

## APPLICATIONS
- Secondary structure prediction.
- Protein function prediction.
- Protein structure modeling.
- Comparative protein analysis.

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- Protein FASTA (.fasta, .fa)
- Protein sequence (.txt)

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Accepts amino acid sequences only.
- Uses sequence-based prediction methods.
- Provides confidence scores for each predicted residue.
- Widely used before tertiary structure prediction.
